---
source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
Stream the logs of one timeline of a run, up to a moment.

A run is a multiverse: a tree of timelines that branch from each other. A
timeline is one continuous simulated execution of the system, and vtime (virtual
time) is its simulated clock. A moment is an instant on a timeline, identified
by an input_hash and a vtime; the input_hash is a hash of every input Antithesis
sent up to that moment. A branch is a timeline that splits off another timeline
at a moment.

INPUT_HASH and VTIME identify a moment. The logs stream along the timeline that
leads to that moment, from its start (or from --begin-vtime) to the moment.
Without VTIME, the stream ends at the last event with INPUT_HASH. A run in
progress can add events, so a later call can return more logs. INPUT_HASH is
often negative, such as `-123`; pass it as it is, with no `--` before it. Find a
moment with `runs properties --detail`, `runs events`, `runs search`, or the
failure moment of an incomplete run in `runs show`.

Each event has a moment, a source, and a payload: log output, an SDK assertion,
a fault, a container lifecycle change, or a test composer command.

Output: a `moment HASH` divider opens the events with each input_hash. The
input_hash changes each time Antithesis sends an input, so the dividers mark the
inputs on the timeline, up to INPUT_HASH. Each event under a divider renders on
one line as `VTIME [source] payload`, each event shape in its own concise form.
VTIME is truncated to fit its column, and a long source label ends in `…`. With
--detail, VTIME and the source print whole, and indented lines under an event
give its source location, as `@ file:function:line`, and the details that it
carries, such as an SDK assertion's details, as `details {...}`.

Add --json for machine-readable output. Each event prints as one JSON object on
its own line:
  snouty --json runs logs <run_id> <hash> | jq -r .moment.vtime

Usage: snouty runs logs [OPTIONS] <RUN_ID> <INPUT_HASH> [VTIME]

Arguments:
  <RUN_ID>
          Run ID

  <INPUT_HASH>
          Input hash of the moment to stream to

  [VTIME]
          Virtual time of the moment to end the stream at; omit it to stream to
          the last event with the input hash

Options:
      --begin-vtime <BEGIN_VTIME>
          Start from this virtual time instead of the root

  -d, --detail
          Detailed rendering: a full-width vtime on every line, source
          locations, and each event's attached details JSON

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
